(Regression test: lists declared from another variable or with no
 initializer. Previously `a list called "b" is the a.` left "b" untyped,
 so "b's length" was misrouted to the file-size fallback and the build
 failed with an undefined _file_size symbol; a bare list declaration
 left a null pointer that the first append dereferenced.)

a list called origin is [10, 20, 30].
a list called mirror is the origin.

Print "origin len: {origin's length}".
Print "mirror len: {mirror's length}".
Print element 2 of mirror.

a list called bare.
append 7 to bare.
append 8 to bare.
Print "bare len: {bare's length}".
Print bare's last.
